 app=['**Expanded valuation appendix — 8September2026**\n','All monetary amounts USD millions unless per share. Forecast numbers are analyst assumptions or calculated consequences. Source-observed history is identified separately. Present value and future exit value are not interchangeable.\n']
 allrows=[]
 for t,r in sorted(results.items(),key=lambda kv:kv[1]['upside'],reverse=True):
  allrows.append([t,money(r['price']),'/'.join(money(r['scenarios'][x]['fair_value_per_share']) for x in ['downside','base','upside']),money(r['probability_weighted_fair_value']),pct(r['upside']),('Unconfirmed' if r.get('unresolved_covenant_shortfall') else pct(r['expected_cashflow_annualized_return'])),('Unconfirmed' if r.get('unresolved_covenant_shortfall') else pct(r['expected_scenario_annualized_return']))])
 app += [table(['Ticker','Price','Down/base/up today','Weighted','Gap','IRR weighted dated proceeds','Mean scenario IRR'],allrows),'Rows above are sorted by modeled gap for transparency, not investment ranking. A complete-loss scenario can make mean scenario IRR negative despite a high return on expected proceeds. GRSD is unconfirmed. The main report weighs financing, evidence and downside.\n',
 '`FCFF = EBIT × (1 − tax rate) + D&A − capex − change in operating working capital`. EBIT retains SBC cost. Annual input revenue is the sum of explicitly modeled segments; group EBIT is segment contribution minus corporate expense. Add five mature-normalization years, then value `terminal FCFF / (WACC − g)`. Mature net reinvestment is the greater of final explicit net investment and `NOPAT × g / ROIC`. Both maintenance and growth spending remain deducted. Nominal USD cash and rates are matched. Initial stub cash is prorated except explicit disclosed-event adjustments.\n',
 'Value common equity as operating EV plus scenario nonoperating asset value and excess cash, less debt/senior claims, floored at zero. For STLA, the captive finance value is a separate distribution DCF after required equity retention; its interim dividends are retained once and its remaining horizon value is added once. Nonoperating dividends are never added to industrial FCFF. Exact known-event stub adjustments replace approximate prorating when specified.\n',
 'Future returns use five-year dated cash distributions and remaining equity value, with no assumed multiple expansion. Actual future recognition remains uncertain;20/40% persistent equity discounts are additional stresses for PDD/VIPS. OPRA/GRSD use detailed dividend/acquisition/debt schedules in extra_model.py; their separate recognition stresses discount operating equity only and are consequently not directly comparable with an entire-equity discount. All future SBC stays economically expensed; no simultaneous dilution double charge. Existing awards and announced acquisition dilution are treated explicitly.\n']
